Skip rules_go's nogo analyzer on go-sqlite3.

nogo runs as a fact-generation action on every Go library — the
go_sdk.nogo `includes`/`excludes` config only controls whether reports
are emitted, not whether the action runs. For CGO packages the action
depends on Bazel-generated cgo intermediates (`_cgo_imports.go` etc.)
which routinely go missing from the remote cache in CI, surfacing as
"Running nogo on @@...com_github_mattn_go_sqlite3//:go-sqlite3 failed:
Missing digest". The `no-nogo` tag suppresses nogo for the target
entirely. See rules_go go/private/actions/archive.bzl:65.

--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
     importpath = "github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3",
+    tags = ["no-nogo"],
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
 )
